            <ArticleTitle>[Localization of the interpleural space using the &quot;hanging drop&quot; method].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>&quot;Hanging drop&quot; method was used in 45 patients to determine interpleural needle placement which was easily achieved in 100% of the cases, advancing a catheter through the needle without any difficulty. No pneumothorax was observed. In conclusion, we consider that &quot;hanging drop&quot; method is effective to determine interpleural needle placement, with little disturbance to the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
